// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/customer_surface.t27 -- what a customer screen may ASSERT, and which tabs he gets
; Two halves of one boundary, and they are the two halves a customer meets before he has typed
; anything. Outward: the home trust block is the only place in the Mini App that makes a claim
; about the shop rather than about an order, and this file owns the CLASSES of claim it may carry
; and the classes it may not. Inward: the tab bar is the whole advertised navigation, and this
; file owns its size and the one rule that makes a tab real -- a tab must resolve to a screen that
; mounts. It owns no wording, no tab label, no locale, no price, no availability figure, no
; configured bot handle and no ruling on whether a legacy surface should go: six sibling
; contracts own those and are named by ID below, not one of them restated.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). DECISIONS.md:384 D20 retargeted the cannabis-era trust block to
; rental facts and wrote the rule in one sentence at :396-397 -- no invented product claims,
; insurance and deposit terms stay the owner's to make. That rule has no enforcer anywhere in the
; repository. The one instrument over this surface is tests/customer_surface_wiring.rs: 820 lines,
; FIFTEEN #[test] functions, and a grep of the whole tests/ directory for T_TRUST returns ZERO.
; Not one of the fifteen reads a claim. What the fifteen do read is navigation -- the tab count at
; :116, the five destinations at :110, five retired route names at :118 -- so the SHAPE of the
; surface is gated to the link and the CONTENT of the surface is gated nowhere. D20's retarget
; could be reversed one key at a time with every one of the fifteen still green.
; --
; THE SECOND MEASUREMENT, and it is why the rule below reads content and never a name. The trust
; block has four claim slots, at src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs:441, :442, :444 and :445-449
; (:437, :438, :440 and :441-445 before the 2026-09-21 cart-price edits added three lines above
; them, and one more on 2026-09-23 when T27 defect 2 gave the order total a serde default; every
; slot was re-read at its new address and carries the same claim). They
; select four keys declared at src/trios/i18n.rs:226-229. THREE of the four keys -- trust.gacp,
; trust.medical, trust.age -- are still named for the claim D20 retired, and all three now carry a
; claim D20 permits: the rows at src/trios/i18n.rs:917-920 and :1517-1520 hold a legal entity with
; a location, a helmet law and a licence requirement. A reader who classified these three rows
; from their key names would refuse all three and admit none, and would be wrong three times. The
; key name is not evidence and this contract never treats it as evidence.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Three corrections, each measured.
;   1. "What the FIRST SCREEN may assert." The first screen is not the screen that carries the
;      trust block. src/ui/routes.rs:103-106 forms has_compatibility_redirect out of four pending
;      deep-link payloads and :110-114 mounts HomeScreen only when one of them is set; an ordinary
;      visit to "/" renders CatalogScreen, which carries no trust block at all (a grep of
;      src/ui/screens/catalog_screen.rs for T_TRUST returns 0). Three of the four mounts then
;      navigate away inside the same effect (src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs:177-193), so the block
;      is a frame in transit; the fourth, the reorder branch at :202-242, awaits a network answer
;      first and leaves the block on screen for as long as that takes -- and for ever if the fetch
;      never resolves. The claims are therefore real, and the surface they live on is a deep-link
;      landing rather than a landing page. Both facts are pinned below.
;   2. "menu_screen.rs ... the five-tab set." /menu is not one of the five. The bar declares five
;      links, at src/ui/components/bottom_nav.rs:25, :32, :39, :46 and :58, and Route::Menu is not
;      among their destinations. It appears in that file once, at :17, as a HIGHLIGHT condition:
;      the fleet tab lights up when the customer is already on /menu, but no tap on the bar can
;      produce it. src/ui/screens/menu_screen.rs:39-43 is a three-line delegation to CatalogScreen.
;      So there are five tabs and EIGHT routes they highlight, and those are two different numbers
;      that a single count would have collapsed.
;   3. "tests/customer_surface_wiring.rs (a source-text scan, not a contract)" is right, and the
;      reason is stronger than the phrasing suggests: src/lib.rs:17-18 declares pub mod ui under
;      #[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")], so cargo test compiles no line of this surface. The scan is
;      not a weaker instrument than a unit test here -- it is the ONLY instrument that exists, and
;      the file says so itself in its own header.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It quotes no copy, in any language: every string on this surface is a
; Russian or English row in src/trios/i18n.rs and is named by the line that declares or selects it,
; never by its wording (L3). No Cyrillic appears anywhere below, and no legal sentence is
; reproduced -- the legal-entity claim is cited as a row, not as text. It carries no tab label. It
; does not rule on whether a legacy surface should be retired or in what order: turbobaby/legacy-
; retirement owns that and its verdict arrives here as one boolean. It decides nothing about what a
; number IS -- turbobaby/pricing-honesty owns the absent-is-not-zero discipline and this file only
; says a screen may not invent one. It restates no locale, no fallback and no key count
; (turbobaby/locale-policy), no deep-link grammar or landing kind (turbobaby/deeplink), no
; stock, rate or bookability figure (turbobaby/availability), and no environment variable, its
; fallback or its resolver (turbobaby/runtime-config, which owns the bot-handle knob and already
; counts this surface's outbound link among the client literals that ignore it). It publishes no
; claim TEXT, so it
; cannot be used to reinstate one. Nothing from D14 -- no renter, handle, phone, key code, plate,
; debt, purchase price or personal note -- in a constant, a comment or a test.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-customer-surface;

pub const KIND : str = "surface-contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/customer-surface";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby customer surface: admissible claims and the tab set";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const DECISIONS : str = "DECISIONS.md D20, stated at :384 and ruled at :394-397";

; --- Sources --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const CLAIM_SURFACE : str = "src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs";
